{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1782021222,"nonce":"dFjhvKUDcymy11cz9SHc67KL4Z4=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABGLVSJQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/303","origin":"github"},"title":"bizzyboat sidescan URDF: add grazing tilt (boresight = half-fan off nadir) — #185 Stage 2","message":"Part of rolker/unh_marine_autonomy#185 (Stage 2 — geometry). Coupled with the `marine_sidescan_mosaic` full-attitude projection sub-issue (filed alongside) — the tilt is only meaningful once the projection stops discarding roll/pitch.\n\n## What\n`bizzyboat_project11/urdf/sensors/sidescan.xacro` currently mounts `_port`/`_starboard` as a pure ±90° rotation about X — **horizontal abeam, no downward tilt** — and the xacro already flags this as a placeholder:\n\n\u003e PLACEHOLDER: side-scan grazing tilt is 0 (port/starboard beams horizontal). Real side-scan fires a few tens of degrees below horizontal — refine … once measured/calibrated.\n\nAdd the **grazing tilt**: pitch `_port`/`_starboard` so the boresight points **`90° − fan/2` off nadir** (SideVü 55° fan → 27.5° off nadir → ~**62.5° depression**), as a **macro param** (e.g. `grazing_deg`) defaulted from the beamwidth. The fan value is now on the wire from the driver (marine_tools#62 / Stage 1: SideVü across-track 55°), so the default is *derived*, not guessed.\n\n## Notes / ramifications\n- **Keep `+X` (forward) horizontal** — apply the depression as a rotation about the across-track axis so the mosaic's heading extraction (`+X` azimuth) is unaffected. Verify against `marine_sidescan_mosaic`.\n- **Benefits**: `rviz_sonar_image` fan + `marine_sonar_to_pointcloud` geometry become physically correct (currently drawn horizontal); and it's the prerequisite mount for the attitude-aware intensity work (#185 Stages 3–4).\n- **Down (ClearVü) frame** stays nadir — unchanged.\n- **Old-bag discontinuity**: recorded bags carry the old horizontal TF; the mosaic (flat-bottom, ignores boresight elevation) is unaffected, but future TF-based intensity work would read the wrong boresight from pre-change bags.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}